# Core #8 (R36-D): a genuine type mismatch on a CONCRETE field of a generic
# struct must be REJECTED at type-check, not silently accepted.
#
# `Expr::FieldAccess` only typed `Defined` receivers; a concrete instantiation
# of a generic struct is `Generic(did, targs)`, which fell through to
# `error_id`. `error_id` unifies with any concrete type, so `String x = p.tag`
# (where `tag` is `int`) passed `gg check` and then CRASHED IR-lowering
# (`AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst: GorgetString) — untracked source consumed`) — an
# int flowing into a String slot. The generic-struct field-access branch now
# returns the concrete field's real type (`int` for `tag`), so the assignment
# mismatch is caught here. (Generic-PARAM fields like `first`/`second` still
# fall through to `error_id` and are typed by monomorphization — the full
# substitution fix is Strategy 2B, tracked in TODO.md.)
struct Pair[A, B]:
    A first
    B second
    int tag

void main():
    Pair[int, String] p = Pair[int, String](1, "x", 7)
    String x = p.tag        # int field assigned to String -> type mismatch
    print(x)
